# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY — this file is never used by the published site.
#
# How it works:
# - .env.local overrides .env when you run the site locally (Vite convention).
# - The published site ignores .env.local (it isn't uploaded) and keeps using
#   the production values in .env / hosting settings.
#
# The browser never holds a Stripe PRIVATE key — private keys live only in the
# backend functions. On localhost those functions use TEST mode automatically
# (see STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY configured server-side). Nothing to set here.
#
# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
